                "text": "I notice the pattern involves pairs of same-colored cells connected by filled lines between them - like the 7s, 3s, 5s, 9s, and 2s each forming a filled segment along their shared row or column. I'm checking whether the fill includes both endpoints inclusively for each pair.\n\nFor the test case: 2s form a column fill between rows 2-8, 4s and 3s fill columns between rows 3-8, 8s fill rows 4-7, and 1s fill row 6 across columns 11-16. When lines intersect, I noticed vertical fills take precedence over horizontal ones based on the training examples - so where the 1s row crosses the 3s column at row6/col12, the 3 wins and gets placed there instead of the 1.",
